===Viridian Gym===
The [[Viridian Gym]] is located on a hill on the north side of town. The building is open, but no one is around. According to an elderly man outside the entrance, the Gym did not have a [[Gym Leader]] until recently, when {{ga|Blue|a young man}} from [[Pallet Town]] took the role. He is often away, however, so challenging the Viridian Gym will need to wait.

===Trainer House===
[[File:Trainer House 1F HGSS.png|thumb|150px|Trainer House, 1F]]
[[File:Trainer House B1F HGSS.png|thumb|150px|Trainer House, B1F]]

The [[Trainer House]] is located in the middle of the city. Built near [[Indigo Plateau]], the ultimate destination for Pokémon Trainers, the Trainer House allows participants to battle in a controlled environment. According to visitors inside the building, only the best Trainers gather here. These Trainers turn out to be real-life people met via the [[Pokéwalker]], and will appear after the accessory is synced with the game. Up to 10 additional Trainers may be encountered this way. Any Pokémon in a Trainer's party above level 50 will have their level reduced to 50. Battles here give no [[experience]] or money, but the player will receive 1 [[Battle Point|BP]] for each victory. If the player has not used the Pokéwalker, the default opponent is {{ga|Cal}}, whose team includes the final forms of each of [[First partner Pokémon|Professor Elm's Pokémon]].

